1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,660
Freelancers offer 2% off if you pay early

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:03,690
all the time.

3
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:06,290
Most never check if it actually makes them money.

4
00:00:07,317 --> 00:00:08,467
This is Terms Desk.

5
00:00:08,977 --> 00:00:10,677
It's an agent that sits on top of PayPal

6
00:00:10,697 --> 00:00:12,307
Invoicing and decides,

7
00:00:12,777 --> 00:00:13,947
invoice by invoice,

8
00:00:14,257 --> 00:00:15,977
whether an early-payment discount earns

9
00:00:15,997 --> 00:00:18,457
you cash, or just hands margin to clients

10
00:00:18,477 --> 00:00:20,007
who'd pay on time anyway.

11
00:00:21,074 --> 00:00:22,164
I press Run agent.

12
00:00:22,714 --> 00:00:24,564
It pulls my draft invoices from PayPal,

13
00:00:24,834 --> 00:00:26,754
scores each client's chance of paying on

14
00:00:26,774 --> 00:00:29,784
time, and passes every proposal to the Skeptic.

15
00:00:30,882 --> 00:00:32,332
The Skeptic is plain math,

16
00:00:32,702 --> 00:00:33,332
not AI.

17
00:00:34,122 --> 00:00:36,972
Lumen Labs pays on time 84% of the time,

18
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:38,842
so a discount would just give away about

19
00:00:38,862 --> 00:00:40,952
$130. Blocked.

20
00:00:41,882 --> 00:00:43,692
Northwind usually pays months late,

21
00:00:43,942 --> 00:00:45,632
so here the discount is worth it.

22
00:00:46,624 --> 00:00:48,694
Nothing goes out until I approve.

23
00:00:49,484 --> 00:00:52,024
One click, and Terms Desk creates the invoice

24
00:00:52,044 --> 00:00:55,204
through the PayPal Invoicing API with a

25
00:00:55,224 --> 00:00:57,434
2% discount and sends it.

26
00:00:57,884 --> 00:01:00,174
If the client misses the 10-day window,

27
00:01:00,484 --> 00:01:02,134
the discount is removed automatically.

28
00:01:02,844 --> 00:01:04,654
And here's the real sandbox payment:

29
00:01:04,804 --> 00:01:08,354
$1,960, marked paid by PayPal.

30
00:01:09,602 --> 00:01:11,152
You can test the rule yourself.

31
00:01:12,102 --> 00:01:14,672
Northwind pays on time 29% of the time,

32
00:01:14,942 --> 00:01:16,652
and the discount comes out positive.

33
00:01:17,222 --> 00:01:19,642
Now raise that chance to 84%.

34
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:21,072
The verdict flips.

35
00:01:21,922 --> 00:01:23,602
Even if every slow payer sped up,

36
00:01:23,622 --> 00:01:25,562
the discount still loses money because you'd

37
00:01:25,582 --> 00:01:27,142
mostly be paying clients who were going

38
00:01:27,162 --> 00:01:28,032
to pay anyway.

39
00:01:29,206 --> 00:01:31,056
Every decision lands in the ledger,

40
00:01:31,386 --> 00:01:33,176
who decided and what it was worth.

41
00:01:33,706 --> 00:01:35,436
Money kept, discounts paid,

42
00:01:35,506 --> 00:01:36,276
nothing hidden.

43
00:01:37,473 --> 00:01:38,303
Terms Desk.

44
00:01:38,733 --> 00:01:40,603
Discounts that earn money, built on PayPal.
